ZCode browser-use plugin
Copyright 2025 Z.ai

This package is an unofficial DeepSeek Harness port of the ZCode built-in
browser-use plugin. The upstream skills and capability documentation are copied
verbatim under skills/ and docs/; their copyright and MIT license remain those
of the original author, and each copied skill carries an added "DSH port note"
section that maps the upstream Node REPL transport onto DSH tools.

Upstream source: /Applications/ZCode.app/Contents/Resources/glm/packages/browser-use-plugin
  .zcode-plugin/plugin.json   name=browser-use, version=0.5.1, license=MIT, author=Z.ai
  skills/control-browser/SKILL.md
  skills/web-gui-tester/SKILL.md
  docs/*                      browser capability documentation
  README.md

Changes required by DSH:
- Upstream drives a `node_repl` MCP server whose `js` tool exposes ZCode's
  `agent.browsers` registry. DSH has no Node REPL host and no in-app browser, so
  the transport is reimplemented as native Playwright-backed tools with the
  `browser_*` names; lib/browser.js and lib/tools.js are new work, not copies.
- The upstream IAB/extension/CDP backend selection, tab-claiming, recording, and
  coordinate (`cua`/`dom_cua`) escapes have no DSH equivalent and are marked as
  inapplicable in the port note.

